-- title:
--   Modular functions with K-rational q-expansion: fixed, with equivariant values
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ (where $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`), and let $\sigma$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\sigma z = z$ for every $z \in K$. Let $g$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar M`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull M` $= \mathbb{Q}(\text{divisorExpansions } M) \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, and assume that the Laurent series underlying $g$ lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver M K`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the constant series attached to elements of $K$ together with the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M`. Write $\sigma$ also for the semilinear automorphism `arithmeticGalois (modularFunctionFieldFull M) σ`, the pair consisting of the coefficientwise map induced by $\sigma$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ and of $\sigma$ itself. Then (1) this semilinear automorphism fixes $g$; and (2) for every place $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a proper valuation subring containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose ideals are principal) which is rational, i.e. whose residue field is generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, one has $(\sigma \cdot V).\mathrm{evalAt}(g) = \sigma(V.\mathrm{evalAt}(g))$, where $\mathrm{evalAt}$ denotes the residue value of $g$ pulled back to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, taken to be $0$ when $g$ is not in the valuation subring.
--
--   This records that the arithmetic (coefficientwise) action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/K)$ on the field of level-$M$ modular functions fixes those functions whose $q$-expansion lies in $K(j(q), j(q^M))$, and that such a function takes Galois-equivariant values at rational places. It is used in the analysis of places on the boundary annuli of the modular curve, where $\sigma$ is taken in an inertia group and $g$ is a node coordinate, so that the quotient $\sigma(g(V))/g(V)$ is a unit whose residue computes a tame character.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_arithmeticGalois_smul_eq_self_and_evalAt_smul_of_coe_mem_fieldOver.lean

